Subject: meson: libresolv is optional

Why: bionic has its resolver in libc and the NDK ships no libresolv, so the required
cc.find_library('resolv') makes meson setup fail for Android.
Source: written for this module from the survey of iputils 20250605 (meson.build); same effect
as the "empty libresolv.a" workaround, without adding a fake library.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -91,7 +91,7 @@
 endif
 
 m_dep = cc.find_library('m')
-resolv_dep = cc.find_library('resolv')
+resolv_dep = cc.find_library('resolv', required : false)
 if cc.has_function('clock_gettime')
 	rt_dep = cc.find_library('disabler-appears-to-disable-executable-build', required : false)
 else
